{"id": 3294999, "title": "CVE-2025-9086: Out of bounds read for cookie path", "submitted": "2025-08-11", "source_url": "https://hackerone.com/reports/3294999", "excerpt": "We are tracking this issue with the public ID `BIGSLEEP-437903454`. Please use this identifier for reference in any future communication.\n\n## **Vulnerability Details**\n\nIn the cookie support found in `cookie.c`, there's an out-of-bounds string comparison that results from a crafted sequence of cookie operations. When saving a new cookie, we check if it should replace an existing cookie for the same domain. We can see in the snippet below that if the previous cookie path is an empty string `\"\",` we'll skip over the NUL-terminator at \\[0\\] and read out-of-bounds when looking for a `/` in the previous cookie path.\n\n```c\nstatic int\nreplace_existing(struct Curl_easy *data,\n                 struct Cookie *co,\n                 struct CookieInfo *ci,\n                 bool secure,\n                 bool *replacep)\n{\n  bool replace_old = FALSE;\n  struct Curl_llist_node *replace_n = NULL;\n  struct Curl_llist_node *n;\n  size_t myhash = cookiehash(co->domain);\n  for(n = Curl_llist_head(&ci->cookielist[myhash]); n; n = Curl_node_next(n)) {\n    struct Cookie *clist = Curl_node_elem(n);\n    if(!strcmp(clist->name, co->name)) {\n      /* the names are identical */\n      bool matching_domains = FALSE;\n\n      if(clist->domain && co->domain) {\n        if(curl_strequal(clist->domain, co->domain))\n          /* The domains are identical */\n          matching_domains = TRUE;\n      }\n      else if(!clist->domain && !co->domain)\n        matching_domains = TRUE;\n\n      if(matching_domains && /* the domains were identical */\n         clist->spath && co->spath && /* both have paths */\n         clist->secure && !co->secure && !secure) {\n        size_t cllen;\n        const char *sep;\n\n        /*\n         * A non-secure cookie may not overlay an existing secure cookie.\n         * For an existing cookie \"a\" with path \"/login\", refuse a new\n         * cookie \"a\" with for example path \"/login/en\", while the path\n         * \"/loginhelper\" is ok.\n         */\n\n        sep = strchr(clist->spath + 1, '/'); // ***0***\n\n        if(sep)\n          cllen = sep - clist->spath;\n        else\n          cllen = strlen(clist->spath);\n\n        if(curl_strnequal(clist->spath, co->spath, cllen)) {\n          infof(data, \"cookie '%s' for domain '%s' dropped, would \"\n                \"overlay an existing cookie\", co->name, co->domain);\n          return CERR_BAD_SECURE;\n        }\u000b\n// ...\n```\n\nIf we look at the cookie ", "excerpt_truncated": true, "final": "policy_question", "final_label": "Needs a policy review", "tone": "warn", "explain": "The code does what the report says, but curl's own policy may exclude it. A maintainer decides.", "confidence": 0.92, "judge_verdict": "likely_invalid", "receipts_override": "the behavior is real; the project's policy section 'NULL dereferences and crashes' may exclude it", "policy_section": "NULL dereferences and crashes", "grounding": {"verdict": "grounded", "rev": "89490b16c736", "rev_source": "tested commit 89490b16c736", "counts": {"grounded": 24, "ungrounded_strong": 0, "ungrounded_medium": 0}, "problems": []}, "summary": "Out-of-bounds read in cookie path replacement when a secure cookie with empty path is replaced by a non-secure cookie.", "claims": [{"id": "C1", "kind": "flaw", "text": "Out-of-bounds string comparison in replace_existing function when previous cookie path is empty", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The code confirms that sanitize_cookie_path('/') returns an empty string (1-byte allocation with only NUL). When replace_existing processes a secure cookie with this empty spath against a non-secure replacement, line 977 executes strchr(clist->spath + 1, '/'), which reads starting at the byte after the NUL terminator — an out-of-bounds read.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/cookie.c", "line": 977, "note": "strchr(clist->spath + 1, '/') reads past NUL when spath is empty string", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/cookie.c", "line": 282, "note": "sanitize_cookie_path returns empty string when input is '/' (len becomes 0 at line 302)", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/cookie.c", "line": 964, "note": "Condition at lines 964-966 allows reaching the vulnerable code when existing cookie is secure with empty path and new cookie is non-secure", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C2", "kind": "location", "text": "Function replace_existing in lib/cookie.c around line 977", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The function exists at the reported location with the quoted code.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/cookie.c", "line": 939, "note": "replace_existing function definition starts at line 939; vulnerable strchr at line 977", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C3", "kind": "trigger", "text": "Replace a secure cookie with empty path by a non-secure cookie on same domain", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The trigger condition matches the report: a secure cookie (set via HTTPS) with empty path, then a non-secure cookie (set via HTTP) on the same domain.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/cookie.c", "line": 964, "note": "Condition requires clist->secure && !co->secure && !secure — exactly the HTTPS-then-HTTP redirect scenario", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C4", "kind": "impact", "text": "Heap buffer overflow due to reading past NUL terminator in strchr", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "ASan confirms a heap-buffer-overflow read at the strchr call. The impact is an out-of-bounds read; the reporter notes no apparent avenue to leak the read data.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/cookie.c", "line": 977, "note": "strchr(clist->spath + 1, '/') reads past the NUL terminator of an empty spath", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/cookie.c", "line": 304, "note": "Curl_memdup0(cookie_path, 0) allocates 1 byte (NUL only) when len==0", "v